@page "/about"
<PageTitle>About · Budget Summary</PageTitle>
<h1 class="page-title">About</h1>

<div class="card">
    <p>
        Final project for the C#/.NET course. Two projects in one repo:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <code>Budget_Summary/</code> - console app with the workflow,
            24 xUnit tests, and the native tax call
        </li>
        <li>
            <code>BudgetSummary.Blazor/</code> - the web UI you're looking at,
            sitting on top of the same core
        </li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        The tax fee is calculated in C. On Linux it's built from
        <code>native/budget_native.c</code> by <code>build.sh</code>. On Windows
        there's a pre-compiled <code>budget_native.dll</code> checked in. The
        Blazor version can't load either one, so it uses
        <code>ManagedTaxFeeAdapter</code> - a straight C# port of the same
        formula, same rounding, same test value.
    </p>

    <p>
        Core logic returns <code>Result&lt;T, DomainError&gt;</code> rather than
        throwing. The scoring rule is a curried function, so the Reports page
        can swap between conservative and aggressive configs without touching
        the runner.
    </p>

    <p>
        <strong>Run the tests:</strong> <code>dotnet test</code><br />
        <strong>Run the UI:</strong> <code>dotnet run --project BudgetSummary.Blazor</code>
    </p>

    <p>
        <a href="https://github.com/TogzhanAITU/SmartWallet" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            Source on GitHub
        </a>
    </p>
</div>